ppose we have an equation of the form\n\n$$\nax=bx\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants. If $a=b,$ then the equation has infinitely many solutions.\n\nNotice that this equation is in the form $ax=bx.$ In this case, \n\n$$\na=p-3,\\,b=4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has infinitely many solutions if\n\n$$\np-3=4.\n$$\n\nSolving this for $p,$ we get\n\n$$\np=7.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186549054 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110720 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c6cd2f04-e0d5-5df0-8e74-ea737501cdf8" :knowledge-point/title "Solving For an Unknown Parameter"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0eab2015-3700-56bf-ac92-fd0a94f661e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548387} {:answer/id #uuid "598ab84f-b8ec-5739-8cb0-fcbd36abfb06" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548519} {:answer/id #uuid "96f6e7b6-efcd-5a03-89c8-76e8676edae9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548648} {:answer/id #uuid "987b69a0-afb9-52c1-b363-d34b352bfb3b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548656} {:answer/id #uuid "f71c8c9c-cd96-5e6e-b046-0e4cdbb2a210" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548847}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "987b69a0-afb9-52c1-b363-d34b352bfb3b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548656} :answer-field/id #uuid "1e0b4382-89cc-5b45-b568-d6f0542bad8f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548879}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d6ec3c46-2316-5f98-be70-c232b5719be1" :question/math-academy-id "q-288560" :question/problem "Consider the equation\n\n$$\n(r-7)x=-x\n$$\n\nwhere $r$ is a constant. Given that this equation has infinitely many solutions, what is the value of $r?$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n\n$$\nax=bx\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants. If $a=b,$ then the equation has infinitely many solutions.\n\nNotice that this equation is in the form $ax=bx.$ In this case, \n\n$$\na=r-7,\\,b=-1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has infinitely many solutions if\n\n$$\nr-7=-1.\n$$\n\nSolving this for $r,$ we get\n\n$$\nr=6.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186549009 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110720 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c6cd2f04-e0d5-5df0-8e74-ea737501cdf8" :knowledge-point/title "Solving For an Unknown Parameter"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2bc56c0e-abb3-5e53-818e-6aa51cc4af57" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548439} {:answer/id #uuid "36c25fee-f58b-5409-a5a6-477628433eda" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548463} {:answer/id #uuid "5ade53e2-0afe-522f-a54b-d5db209e2043" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548522} {:answer/id #uuid "6e3dbfdf-aa6d-5049-8e76-3fb7df01f4ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548560} {:answer/id #uuid "7e1a1e15-d44d-54e8-a331-6ddc82706537" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548595}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7e1a1e15-d44d-54e8-a331-6ddc82706537" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548595} :answer-field/id #uuid "e27fc349-c24d-5039-a135-0c2dd2d434ed" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548967}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "61992611-6e48-5a2e-9a4c-b280b994c51d" :question/math-academy-id "q-288561" :question/problem "Consider the equation\n\n$$\n(t+4)x=2x\n$$\n\nwhere $t$ is a constant. Given that this equation has infinitely many solutions, what is the value of $t?$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n\n$$\nax=bx\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants. If $a=b,$ then the equation has infinitely many solutions.\n\nNotice that this equation is in the form $ax=bx.$ In this case, \n\n$$\na=t+4,\\,b=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has infinitely many solutions if\n\n$$\nt+4=2.\n$$\n\nSolving this for $t,$ we get\n\n$$\nt=-2.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297195 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110721 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4b1fd794-f42b-5316-80e9-0698cb1f8b87" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a General Equation With Infinitely Many Solutions For Unknown Parameters"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fe4c39bf-4560-5825-a22a-76a5df230cbf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296621}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fe4c39bf-4560-5825-a22a-76a5df230cbf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296621} :answer-field/id #uuid "58355121-2d5d-5aa8-91c2-79f41befa005" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296811}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c1e37e75-7d0c-5923-8a40-5f706dc21da1" :question/math-academy-id "q-288584" :question/problem "Consider the equation\n\n$$\n(-s+3)x+2t=x+6\n$$\n\nwhere $s$ and $t$ are constants. Given that this equation has infinitely many solutions, what is the value of $s+t?$\n\n$s+t=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n\n$$\nax+b=cx+d\n$$\n\nwhere $a,b,c,$ and $d$ are constants. This equation has infinitely many solutions if \n\n$$\na=c\\,\\text{and}\\,b=d.\n$$\n\nTo determine the values of $s$ and $t$ such that the equation\n\n$$\n(-s+3)x+2t=x+6\n$$\n\nhas infinitely many solutions, we equate the coefficients of $x,$ and we equate the constants:\n\n- Equating the coefficients of $x,$ we have\n\n$$\n-s+3=1.\n$$\n\nSolving this equation for $s,$ we get\n\n$$\ns=2.\n$$\n\n- Equating the constants, we have\n\n$$\n2t=6.\n$$\n\nSolving this equation for $t,$ we get\n\n$$\nt=3.\n$$\n\nFinally, since $s=2$ and $t=3,$ we have\n\n$$\ns+t=2+3=5.\n$$"}]}
